    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-1-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 At the end of section 315A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-1-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) However, if:\n\n(a) a *proceeds of crime authority applies for a *forfeiture order\nrelating to particular property; and\n\n(b) a person applies for an order (the exclusion order) under\nsection 29 or 29A to exclude a specified *interest in that\nproperty from a *restraining order; and\n\n(c) the application for the exclusion order has not been\nwithdrawn;\nthe court may only hear the application for the forfeiture order after\nthe application for the exclusion order has been determined.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(2) However, if:\n\n(a) a *proceeds of crime authority applies for a *forfeiture order\nrelating to particular property; and\n\n(b) a person applies for an order (the exclusion order) under\nsection 29 or 29A to exclude a specified *interest in that\nproperty from a *restraining order; and\n\n(c) the application for the exclusion order has not been\nwithdrawn;\nthe court may only hear the application for the forfeiture order after\nthe application for the exclusion order has been determined.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-1-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-1-sec-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "910f57d009526c010f6f93fe0c32bcb6a7a37d1ba5d8a788c0084129041ad2a1",
      "skos:note": "Court may only hear application for forfeiture order after exclusion order has been determined."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-1-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 At the end of section 315A",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(2) However, if:\n\n(a) a *proceeds of crime authority applies for a *forfeiture order\nrelating to particular property; and\n\n(b) a person applies for an order (the exclusion order) under\nsection 29 or 29A to exclude a specified *interest in that\nproperty from a *restraining order; and\n\n(c) the application for the exclusion order has not been\nwithdrawn;\nthe court may only hear the application for the forfeiture order after\nthe application for the exclusion order has been determined."
    },
    {
