    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-2-sec-490-2-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "490(4) 2  Reckless false dealing with accounting documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-2-sec-490-2-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(4) An offence against this section committed by a body corporate is\npunishable on conviction by a fine not more than the greatest of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) 50,000 penalty units;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the conduct constituting the\noffence—1.5 times the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—5% of\nthe annual turnover of the body corporate during the period\n(the turnover period) of 12 months ending at the end of the\nmonth in which the conduct constituting the offence\noccurred.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) An offence against this section committed by a body corporate is\npunishable on conviction by a fine not more than the greatest of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) 50,000 penalty units;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the conduct constituting the\noffence—1.5 times the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—5% of\nthe annual turnover of the body corporate during the period\n(the turnover period) of 12 months ending at the end of the\nmonth in which the conduct constituting the offence\noccurred.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-2-sec-490-2"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-2-sec-490-2-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-2-sec-490-2-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "de63ec7098793872c6eb34492754799b036bdd6144c5e45dbe5635047a9705d4",
      "skos:note": "Offence against section 490(4) punishable by fine"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-2-sec-490-2-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "490(4) 2  Reckless false dealing with accounting documents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(4) An offence against this section committed by a body corporate is\npunishable on conviction by a fine not more than the greatest of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) 50,000 penalty units;\n\n(b) if the court can determine the value of the benefit that the\nbody corporate, and any body corporate related to the body\ncorporate, have obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the conduct constituting the\noffence—1.5 times the value of that benefit;\n\n(c) if the court cannot determine the value of that benefit—5% of\nthe annual turnover of the body corporate during the period\n(the turnover period) of 12 months ending at the end of the\nmonth in which the conduct constituting the offence\noccurred."
    },
