    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-2-sec-490-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "490 6  Consent to commencement of proceedings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-2-sec-490-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Division must not be\ncommenced without the Attorney-General’s written consent if:\n\n(a) the conduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly in\na foreign country; and\n\nFalse accounting  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 15, 2016\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other\nMeasures) Act 2016\n\n(b) at the time of the alleged offence, the person alleged to have\ncommitted the offence is none of the following:\n\n(i) an Australian citizen;\n\n(ii) a resident of Australia;\n\n(iii) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) However, a person may be arrested for, charged with, or remanded\nin custody or released on bail in connection with an offence against\nthis Division before the necessary consent has been given.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Division must not be\ncommenced without the Attorney-General’s written consent if:\n\n(a) the conduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly in\na foreign country; and\n\nFalse accounting  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 15, 2016\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other\nMeasures) Act 2016\n\n(b) at the time of the alleged offence, the person alleged to have\ncommitted the offence is none of the following:\n\n(i) an Australian citizen;\n\n(ii) a resident of Australia;\n\n(iii) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) However, a person may be arrested for, charged with, or remanded\nin custody or released on bail in connection with an offence against\nthis Division before the necessary consent has been given.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-2-sec-490-6-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-2-sec-490-6-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a5a05d5bb19ea5062495f6e6808b925cdb050e56ff6c3d1034adf11f791287fa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-2-sec-490-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "490 6  Consent to commencement of proceedings",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings for an offence against this Division must not be\ncommenced without the Attorney-General’s written consent if:\n\n(a) the conduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly in\na foreign country; and\n\nFalse accounting  Schedule 2\n\nNo. 15, 2016\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other\nMeasures) Act 2016\n\n(b) at the time of the alleged offence, the person alleged to have\ncommitted the offence is none of the following:\n\n(i) an Australian citizen;\n\n(ii) a resident of Australia;\n\n(iii) a body corporate incorporated by or under a law of the\nCommonwealth or of a State or Territory.\n\n(2) However, a person may be arrested for, charged with, or remanded\nin custody or released on bail in connection with an offence against\nthis Division before the necessary consent has been given."
    },
