      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-3-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Subsection 301.9(2) of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-3-sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) The following groups and atoms are specified:\n\n(a) alkoxy, cyclic diether, acyl, acyloxy, mono-amino or\ndialkylamino groups with up to 6 carbon atoms in any alkyl\nresidue;\n\n(b) alkyl, alkenyl or alkynyl groups with up to 6 carbon atoms in\nthe group, where the group is attached to oxygen (for\nexample, an ester or an ether group), nitrogen, sulphur or\ncarbon;\n\n(c) halogen, hydroxy, nitro or amino groups;\n\n(d) hydrogen atoms.\n\n(3) However:\n\n(a) a drug analogue of a listed controlled drug does not include a\nsubstance that is itself a listed controlled drug; and\n\n(b) a drug analogue of a listed border controlled drug does not\ninclude a substance that is itself a listed border controlled\ndrug.\n\n(4) In this section:\naddition has its ordinary meaning.\nreplacement has its ordinary meaning.\n\nSerious drugs  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 15, 2016\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other\nMeasures) Act 2016",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) The following groups and atoms are specified:\n\n(a) alkoxy, cyclic diether, acyl, acyloxy, mono-amino or\ndialkylamino groups with up to 6 carbon atoms in any alkyl\nresidue;\n\n(b) alkyl, alkenyl or alkynyl groups with up to 6 carbon atoms in\nthe group, where the group is attached to oxygen (for\nexample, an ester or an ether group), nitrogen, sulphur or\ncarbon;\n\n(c) halogen, hydroxy, nitro or amino groups;\n\n(d) hydrogen atoms.\n\n(3) However:\n\n(a) a drug analogue of a listed controlled drug does not include a\nsubstance that is itself a listed controlled drug; and\n\n(b) a drug analogue of a listed border controlled drug does not\ninclude a substance that is itself a listed border controlled\ndrug.\n\n(4) In this section:\naddition has its ordinary meaning.\nreplacement has its ordinary meaning.\n\nSerious drugs  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 15, 2016\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other\nMeasures) Act 2016",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-3-sec-3-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-3-sec-3-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-3-sec-3-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016#sch-3-sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Subsection 301.9(2) of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(2) The following groups and atoms are specified:\n\n(a) alkoxy, cyclic diether, acyl, acyloxy, mono-amino or\ndialkylamino groups with up to 6 carbon atoms in any alkyl\nresidue;\n\n(b) alkyl, alkenyl or alkynyl groups with up to 6 carbon atoms in\nthe group, where the group is attached to oxygen (for\nexample, an ester or an ether group), nitrogen, sulphur or\ncarbon;\n\n(c) halogen, hydroxy, nitro or amino groups;\n\n(d) hydrogen atoms.\n\n(3) However:\n\n(a) a drug analogue of a listed controlled drug does not include a\nsubstance that is itself a listed controlled drug; and\n\n(b) a drug analogue of a listed border controlled drug does not\ninclude a substance that is itself a listed border controlled\ndrug.\n\n(4) In this section:\naddition has its ordinary meaning.\nreplacement has its ordinary meaning.\n\nSerious drugs  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 15, 2016\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other\nMeasures) Act 2016"
    },
